{"id":155617549,"slug":"does-adult-adhd-lead-to-early-death","title":"Does Adult ADHD Lead to Early Death? Spoiler Alert: Yes.","subtitle":"Are we missing something when it comes to morbidity and mortality in ADHD?","post_date":"2025-01-27T14:08:46.805Z","audience":"everyone","type":"newsletter","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/does-adult-adhd-lead-to-early-death","wordcount":949,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T21:49:11.738Z","body_sha256":"71bf8d90c1f59296e58d46784f1dcaf8c661907f4a815862fb6453147f77fe56","text_words":1013,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p>The Frontier Psychiatrists is a daily enough health-themed newsletter.  Some of our <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/what-is-adult-adhd?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\">most popular articles are about ADHD. </a> This disorder has a storied history and has had several monikers over the years.  In the earlier 20th century, we referred to it as <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/793563/\">minimal brain dysfunction</a>. Subsequently, we had attention deficit disorder.  Then, most recently, attention deficit <em>hyperactivity</em> disorder was added. This, in turn, has three identified subtypes: inattentive, hyperactive, and combined, where you have both hyperactivity and inattentive symptoms.  </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dzP9!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6b05ec7-75d2-4c32-aeb3-126e340545eb_2348x1408.heic\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dzP9!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6b05ec7-75d2-4c32-aeb3-126e340545eb_2348x1408.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dzP9!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6b05ec7-75d2-4c32-aeb3-126e340545eb_2348x1408.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dzP9!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6b05ec7-75d2-4c32-aeb3-126e340545eb_2348x1408.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dzP9!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6b05ec7-75d2-4c32-aeb3-126e340545eb_2348x1408.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dzP9!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6b05ec7-75d2-4c32-aeb3-126e340545eb_2348x1408.heic\" width=\"537\" height=\"321.9787087912088\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/d6b05ec7-75d2-4c32-aeb3-126e340545eb_2348x1408.heic&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:873,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:537,&quot;bytes&quot;:41550,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/heic&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dzP9!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6b05ec7-75d2-4c32-aeb3-126e340545eb_2348x1408.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dzP9!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6b05ec7-75d2-4c32-aeb3-126e340545eb_2348x1408.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dzP9!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6b05ec7-75d2-4c32-aeb3-126e340545eb_2348x1408.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dzP9!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6b05ec7-75d2-4c32-aeb3-126e340545eb_2348x1408.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">That “<strong>difference</strong>” is “years of life people with ADHD don’t get to stay alive for.”</figcaption></figure></div><p>It's even gotten so popular that we have “made-up” diagnoses—essentially, individuals advocating for new diagnostic entities that are not yet in the pantheon of the International Classification of Disease (ICD) or the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual for Mental Disorders (DSM-5-TR); it's kind of like the farm leagues for diagnosis?  But we have conceptualizations like “rejection sensitivity dysphoria” or RSD, as a maybe an ADHD subtype.  We've got endless TikTok videos. We've got ads where people misspell things on purpose to lure in those with ADHD for <em>some kind of scam.</em></p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Gnc0!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe9108a80-21df-4e8a-b1dc-878275fc4418_656x626.heic\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Gnc0!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe9108a80-21df-4e8a-b1dc-878275fc4418_656x626.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Gnc0!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe9108a80-21df-4e8a-b1dc-878275fc4418_656x626.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Gnc0!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe9108a80-21df-4e8a-b1dc-878275fc4418_656x626.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Gnc0!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe9108a80-21df-4e8a-b1dc-878275fc4418_656x626.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Gnc0!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe9108a80-21df-4e8a-b1dc-878275fc4418_656x626.heic\" width=\"346\" height=\"330.1768292682927\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/e9108a80-21df-4e8a-b1dc-878275fc4418_656x626.heic&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:626,&quot;width&quot;:656,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:346,&quot;bytes&quot;:58263,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/heic&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Gnc0!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe9108a80-21df-4e8a-b1dc-878275fc4418_656x626.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Gnc0!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe9108a80-21df-4e8a-b1dc-878275fc4418_656x626.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Gnc0!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe9108a80-21df-4e8a-b1dc-878275fc4418_656x626.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Gnc0!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe9108a80-21df-4e8a-b1dc-878275fc4418_656x626.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Perplexing internet scams.</figcaption></figure></div><p>A pedantic point: RESPONCE is not how you spell the word RESPONSE.  My hunch is this is part of a scam sales funnel that selects for individuals who are paying no attention to the details.  To be clear, is the claim that “hypersexuality is not infidelity [but instead part of ADHD]” factual?  <em>This is not a thing—</em>except, perhaps, as clickbait.  </p><p>Moving on, we've covered here how ADHD—specifically stimulant medications—is associated with morbidity in ADHD.  Allow me to summarize my now-classic (<em>according to me alone</em>) treatise, “<a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/is-my-adhd-medication-killing-me?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\">Is My ADHD Medication Killing Me?</a>”:</p><blockquote><p>Yes, your ADHD medication might kill you. But, it’s more likely your ADHD will kill you on it’s own if left untreated. The deaths happen early, and the risks happen late.</p></blockquote><p>While that is true about the medicines themselves, today’s publication in the British Medical Journal is an epidemiological study, following millions of people over about 20 years, evaluating the rate of early death in individuals diagnosed with ADHD.</p><p>With any study, my first question is “Who is in the sample.”  As I frequently joke, this newsletter could be renamed. “<a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/how-to-read-academic-research-like?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\">The Table One Star-Ledger</a>.”  The first table in an academic research paper in biomedical science, Table One, reviews the question of who is in the sample.  Here, we find the following:</p><blockquote><p>A matched cohort study using prospectively collected primary care data (792 general practices, 9 561 450 people contributing eligible person-time from 2000–2019). We identified <strong>30 039 people aged 18+ with diagnosed ADHD</strong>, plus a comparison group of 300 390 participants matched (1:10) by age, sex, and primary care practice. We used Poisson regression to estimate age-specific mortality rates, and life tables to estimate life expectancy for people aged 18+ with diagnosed ADHD.<a class=\"footnote-anchor\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteAnchorToDOM\" id=\"footnote-anchor-1\" href=\"#footnote-1\" target=\"_self\">1</a></p></blockquote><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/does-adult-adhd-lead-to-early-death?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/does-adult-adhd-lead-to-early-death?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p><p>If we dig in further, readers may ask, is there more we could understand?  So glad you asked.</p><div class=\"paywall-jump\" data-component-name=\"PaywallToDOM\"></div><p>They matched 30,000 ADHD-diagnosed individuals with 300,000 participants who didn't have ADHD. The authors review, retrospectively, what occurred as time elapsed.   <a href=\"http://control\">My erudite review of cohort and case-control studies is available here.</a>  Allow me to save you heartache—this study design won’t tell us why people died early.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OWvr!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F60fa4d07-7e9a-4257-ba0a-c9fc1b54ece0_1816x910.heic\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OWvr!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F60fa4d07-7e9a-4257-ba0a-c9fc1b54ece0_1816x910.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OWvr!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F60fa4d07-7e9a-4257-ba0a-c9fc1b54ece0_1816x910.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OWvr!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F60fa4d07-7e9a-4257-ba0a-c9fc1b54ece0_1816x910.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OWvr!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F60fa4d07-7e9a-4257-ba0a-c9fc1b54ece0_1816x910.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OWvr!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F60fa4d07-7e9a-4257-ba0a-c9fc1b54ece0_1816x910.heic\" width=\"1456\" height=\"730\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/60fa4d07-7e9a-4257-ba0a-c9fc1b54ece0_1816x910.heic&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:730,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:131675,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/heic&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OWvr!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F60fa4d07-7e9a-4257-ba0a-c9fc1b54ece0_1816x910.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OWvr!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F60fa4d07-7e9a-4257-ba0a-c9fc1b54ece0_1816x910.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OWvr!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F60fa4d07-7e9a-4257-ba0a-c9fc1b54ece0_1816x910.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OWvr!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F60fa4d07-7e9a-4257-ba0a-c9fc1b54ece0_1816x910.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>You will quickly see that the percentage of death was higher in the ADHD groups for both men and women —and quite a bit higher for women with ADHD.</p><p>They then examined the rates of disorders that co-occurred with ADHD versus the matched population in over the time period in question:</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wOig!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F73be57d7-616c-44ab-9f20-35e97001caa7_1816x840.heic\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wOig!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F73be57d7-616c-44ab-9f20-35e97001caa7_1816x840.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wOig!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F73be57d7-616c-44ab-9f20-35e97001caa7_1816x840.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wOig!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F73be57d7-616c-44ab-9f20-35e97001caa7_1816x840.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wOig!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F73be57d7-616c-44ab-9f20-35e97001caa7_1816x840.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wOig!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F73be57d7-616c-44ab-9f20-35e97001caa7_1816x840.heic\" width=\"1456\" height=\"673\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/73be57d7-616c-44ab-9f20-35e97001caa7_1816x840.heic&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:673,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:153514,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/heic&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wOig!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F73be57d7-616c-44ab-9f20-35e97001caa7_1816x840.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wOig!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F73be57d7-616c-44ab-9f20-35e97001caa7_1816x840.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wOig!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F73be57d7-616c-44ab-9f20-35e97001caa7_1816x840.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wOig!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F73be57d7-616c-44ab-9f20-35e97001caa7_1816x840.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>We will notice in individuals with ADHD there are some significant differences in other problems they have. Smoking rates are vastly higher. Alcohol abuse is vastly higher, and there are significantly higher rates of suicide attempts <em>by a factor of 10 times</em>, and even personality disorders are orders of magnitude more prominent.  It seems that people with ADHD have <em>other problems</em>. It's not hypercholesterolemia; although it is a bit more prominent, we have some real drivers of badness for a less long, healthy life.</p><p>Thus, at <em>almost</em> every age group for men and at <em>every age group for women</em>, humans with ADHD are more likely to die and more likely to die younger:</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XZ9k!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbdcb0cd8-2f7d-4490-9b30-b6156758072e_2476x1078.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XZ9k!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbdcb0cd8-2f7d-4490-9b30-b6156758072e_2476x1078.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XZ9k!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbdcb0cd8-2f7d-4490-9b30-b6156758072e_2476x1078.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XZ9k!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbdcb0cd8-2f7d-4490-9b30-b6156758072e_2476x1078.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XZ9k!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbdcb0cd8-2f7d-4490-9b30-b6156758072e_2476x1078.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XZ9k!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbdcb0cd8-2f7d-4490-9b30-b6156758072e_2476x1078.png\" width=\"529\" height=\"230.34752747252747\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/bdcb0cd8-2f7d-4490-9b30-b6156758072e_2476x1078.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:634,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:529,&quot;bytes&quot;:612728,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XZ9k!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbdcb0cd8-2f7d-4490-9b30-b6156758072e_2476x1078.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XZ9k!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbdcb0cd8-2f7d-4490-9b30-b6156758072e_2476x1078.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XZ9k!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbdcb0cd8-2f7d-4490-9b30-b6156758072e_2476x1078.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XZ9k!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbdcb0cd8-2f7d-4490-9b30-b6156758072e_2476x1078.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Mortality rates at different ages.  ADHD in the dark blue on top.</figcaption></figure></div><p>ADHD predicted early death, among both men and women.</p><blockquote><p>The apparent reduction in life expectancy for adults with diagnosed ADHD relative to the general population was <strong>6.78 years</strong> (95% CI: 4.50 to 9.11) for males, and <strong>8.64 years</strong> (95% CI: 6.55 to 10.91) for females.</p></blockquote><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!boUn!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01972aec-f5d8-4d52-a725-7c1e831918b0_1814x580.heic\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!boUn!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01972aec-f5d8-4d52-a725-7c1e831918b0_1814x580.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!boUn!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01972aec-f5d8-4d52-a725-7c1e831918b0_1814x580.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!boUn!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01972aec-f5d8-4d52-a725-7c1e831918b0_1814x580.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!boUn!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01972aec-f5d8-4d52-a725-7c1e831918b0_1814x580.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!boUn!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01972aec-f5d8-4d52-a725-7c1e831918b0_1814x580.heic\" width=\"1456\" height=\"466\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/01972aec-f5d8-4d52-a725-7c1e831918b0_1814x580.heic&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:466,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:70479,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/heic&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!boUn!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01972aec-f5d8-4d52-a725-7c1e831918b0_1814x580.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!boUn!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01972aec-f5d8-4d52-a725-7c1e831918b0_1814x580.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!boUn!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01972aec-f5d8-4d52-a725-7c1e831918b0_1814x580.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!boUn!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01972aec-f5d8-4d52-a725-7c1e831918b0_1814x580.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>These findings don’t tell us WHY people with ADHD are dying earlier.  Cohort studies can’t demonstrate causality.  They are hypothesis generating, only.  However, the data make it clear that ADHD is a threat not only to quality of life, but to life itself, over a long enough time scale.  </p><p>This is serious, impacts women more, and thus should be an area of ongoing and robust inquiry and public health focus.  Let’s not let people die earlier than they need to—they have lives and families.  We need to keep ADHDers around, healthy, and happy.  I say this both as a physician and as someone who has ADHD that, I now know, predicts my early death.  For my family too, I beg my colleagues—let’s focus on reducing the risks while ensuring long, healthy lives for all of us.</p><p>Given we are not sure why these early deaths occurred, perhaps we encourage ADHD sufferers to get all the close follow up to which they are other wise entitled.  Get serious about alcohol use disorder, smoking cessation, and other preventable causes of death.</p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">The Frontier Psychiatrists is a reader-supported publication. To receive new posts and support my work, consider becoming a free or paid subscriber.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/does-adult-adhd-lead-to-early-death?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/does-adult-adhd-lead-to-early-death?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p><p></p><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-1\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-1\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">1</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>O’Nions E, El Baou C, John A, et al. Life expectancy and years of life lost for adults with diagnosed ADHD in the UK: matched cohort study. <em>The British Journal of Psychiatry</em>. Published online 2025:1-8. doi:10.1192/bjp.2024.199</p><p></p></div></div>","text":"The Frontier Psychiatrists is a daily enough health-themed newsletter. Some of our most popular articles are about ADHD. This disorder has a storied history and has had several monikers over the years. In the earlier 20th century, we referred to it as minimal brain dysfunction . Subsequently, we had attention deficit disorder. Then, most recently, attention deficit hyperactivity disorder was added. This, in turn, has three identified subtypes: inattentive, hyperactive, and combined, where you have both hyperactivity and inattentive symptoms.\n\nThat “ difference ” is “years of life people with ADHD don’t get to stay alive for.”\n\nIt's even gotten so popular that we have “made-up” diagnoses—essentially, individuals advocating for new diagnostic entities that are not yet in the pantheon of the International Classification of Disease (ICD) or the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual for Mental Disorders (DSM-5-TR); it's kind of like the farm leagues for diagnosis? But we have conceptualizations like “rejection sensitivity dysphoria” or RSD, as a maybe an ADHD subtype. We've got endless TikTok videos. We've got ads where people misspell things on purpose to lure in those with ADHD for some kind of scam.\n\nPerplexing internet scams.\n\nA pedantic point: RESPONCE is not how you spell the word RESPONSE. My hunch is this is part of a scam sales funnel that selects for individuals who are paying no attention to the details. To be clear, is the claim that “hypersexuality is not infidelity [but instead part of ADHD]” factual? This is not a thing— except, perhaps, as clickbait.\n\nMoving on, we've covered here how ADHD—specifically stimulant medications—is associated with morbidity in ADHD. Allow me to summarize my now-classic ( according to me alone ) treatise, “ Is My ADHD Medication Killing Me? ”:\n\nYes, your ADHD medication might kill you. But, it’s more likely your ADHD will kill you on it’s own if left untreated. The deaths happen early, and the risks happen late.\n\nWhile that is true about the medicines themselves, today’s publication in the British Medical Journal is an epidemiological study, following millions of people over about 20 years, evaluating the rate of early death in individuals diagnosed with ADHD.\n\nWith any study, my first question is “Who is in the sample.” As I frequently joke, this newsletter could be renamed. “ The Table One Star-Ledger .” The first table in an academic research paper in biomedical science, Table One, reviews the question of who is in the sample. Here, we find the following:\n\nA matched cohort study using prospectively collected primary care data (792 general practices, 9 561 450 people contributing eligible person-time from 2000–2019). We identified 30 039 people aged 18+ with diagnosed ADHD , plus a comparison group of 300 390 participants matched (1:10) by age, sex, and primary care practice. We used Poisson regression to estimate age-specific mortality rates, and life tables to estimate life expectancy for people aged 18+ with diagnosed ADHD. 1\n\nShare\n\nIf we dig in further, readers may ask, is there more we could understand? So glad you asked.\n\nThey matched 30,000 ADHD-diagnosed individuals with 300,000 participants who didn't have ADHD. The authors review, retrospectively, what occurred as time elapsed. My erudite review of cohort and case-control studies is available here. Allow me to save you heartache—this study design won’t tell us why people died early.\n\nYou will quickly see that the percentage of death was higher in the ADHD groups for both men and women —and quite a bit higher for women with ADHD.\n\nThey then examined the rates of disorders that co-occurred with ADHD versus the matched population in over the time period in question:\n\nWe will notice in individuals with ADHD there are some significant differences in other problems they have. Smoking rates are vastly higher. Alcohol abuse is vastly higher, and there are significantly higher rates of suicide attempts by a factor of 10 times , and even personality disorders are orders of magnitude more prominent. It seems that people with ADHD have other problems . It's not hypercholesterolemia; although it is a bit more prominent, we have some real drivers of badness for a less long, healthy life.\n\nThus, at almost every age group for men and at every age group for women , humans with ADHD are more likely to die and more likely to die younger:\n\nMortality rates at different ages. ADHD in the dark blue on top.\n\nADHD predicted early death, among both men and women.\n\nThe apparent reduction in life expectancy for adults with diagnosed ADHD relative to the general population was 6.78 years (95% CI: 4.50 to 9.11) for males, and 8.64 years (95% CI: 6.55 to 10.91) for females.\n\nThese findings don’t tell us WHY people with ADHD are dying earlier. Cohort studies can’t demonstrate causality. They are hypothesis generating, only. However, the data make it clear that ADHD is a threat not only to quality of life, but to life itself, over a long enough time scale.\n\nThis is serious, impacts women more, and thus should be an area of ongoing and robust inquiry and public health focus. Let’s not let people die earlier than they need to—they have lives and families. We need to keep ADHDers around, healthy, and happy. I say this both as a physician and as someone who has ADHD that, I now know, predicts my early death. For my family too, I beg my colleagues—let’s focus on reducing the risks while ensuring long, healthy lives for all of us.\n\nGiven we are not sure why these early deaths occurred, perhaps we encourage ADHD sufferers to get all the close follow up to which they are other wise entitled. Get serious about alcohol use disorder, smoking cessation, and other preventable causes of death.\n\nThe Frontier Psychiatrists is a reader-supported publication. To receive new posts and support my work, consider becoming a free or paid subscriber.\n\nShare\n\n1 O’Nions E, El Baou C, John A, et al. Life expectancy and years of life lost for adults with diagnosed ADHD in the UK: matched cohort study. The British Journal of Psychiatry . Published online 2025:1-8. doi:10.1192/bjp.2024.199"}